VERDICT
  75 MHz (13.333 ns, the KV260 board budget -- "slack in the target
  configuration"): MET by all five profiles, smallest margin +1.753 ns
  (eonly). Vivado's own line in each report: "All user specified timing
  constraints are met."
  200 MHz (5.0 ns, headroom probe): MET by featparity_gold (+0.339 ns) and
  slimfull_gold (+0.362 ns); NOT met by the three full-profile builds
  (voll_gold / nonly -4.158 ns, eonly -6.580 ns). That is a result, not a
  failure: 200 MHz is not a requirement anywhere in this project.

