CONTROLS THAT CAME OUT OF THE RUN ITSELF
  * nonly and voll_gold are the SAME build: the two profile definitions
    produce a byte-identical rtl/pkg/ct_pkg.sv (checked before the runs), and
    the two independent synthesis runs then agree on every figure including
    TNS (-2262.302) and the failing-endpoint count (2777). The protocol pair
    is therefore N-only = the committed full profile, E-only = the same
    profile with the back-end selector flipped -- which is how P9 measured it.
  * voll_gold @ 75 MHz was synthesized twice, once at 8678011 and once at
    7a0b7b2 (comment-only commits apart): WNS 4.175, 25784 LUTs, 20168 FFs
    both times. The filed report is the pinned one.
  * Utilization is budget-independent by construction (the constraints are
    applied after synth_design), and the two runs of each profile confirm it
    to the LUT -- so each profile's two util_flat reports are a
    reproducibility control on the synthesis, not a duplicate.

WHAT THIS NUMBER IS NOT
  Out-of-context synthesis of ct_encoder alone, with one clock per clock port
  at the same budget and set_clock_groups -asynchronous between them (the
  encoder's CDC structures are exactly what a real SoC XDC decouples the same
  way). It is therefore NOT a placed-and-routed figure, and cross-domain paths
  are excluded from the analysis by that constraint. The only P&R number this
  project has is the mbv_kv260 reference design of 2026-08-01 (WNS +2.186 ns
  at 75 MHz), which predates P2..P9 and is marked historical in the
  documentation.

